==Strategy==
A fairly difficult [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] stage if one is unprepared. Players must bring a mix of [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|critical hitters]] and [[:Category:anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie Cats]] for effectiveness against both Cyclones. Remember that these two Cyclones are not Floating, so anti-Floating units are useless.

Wait until the first Metal Doge spawns and lure it to the base, then use it to stack a ton of crowd control units before deploying the first crit unit. This should allow enough units to be built up to consistently stop the cyclones.

It is a good idea to try and destroy the Metal Cyclone before the Zyclone reaches your front line, though very good luck is needed. [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]] is very effective for critical hits against the Metal Cyclone, but its long attack animation and cooldown means it must be protected extraordinarily well. [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] is also a good option. [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan Pasalan]] can one-shot the Metal Cyclone, but be wary of its low crit rate and single target.

Bringing [[:Category:anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal Cats]] like [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoopmaster Cat]] and [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Puppetmaster & Charley]] can help keep the Metal Cyclone controlled for more accurate critical hits, but caution must be taken that the Zyclone doesn't disrupt this. Thus, anti-Zombie units must be deployed at the same time if the cyclones both reach your front line. [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]] is very useful to knock back the Zyclone if it reaches your front lines, and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] can slow the Zyclone to allow you to focus the Metal Cyclone.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant Poseidon]]: He's basically made for this stage as he is able to freeze all units on the field from a distance.
*[[Mech Patrol Axel (Uber Rare Cat)|Steel Sergeant Axel]]: His Conjure and Metal Killer can drastically reduce Metal Cyclone's HP especially at the beginning. He can't do much for Zyclone, however, and also requires good meatshielding or support to avoid the cyclones pushing into his blindspot.
*[[Jack Hammer (Uber Rare Cat)|Jack Hammer]]: Works in a similar fashion to Axel's second form in how he rips off significant portions of Metal Cyclone's HP, except he doesn't have a blindspot and also has Zombie Killer to be able to finish off Zyclone as well, though he doesn't deal much damage to do so by himself. He also carries Weaken procs against both traits, which while not too impactful for the cyclones' insane DPS it can still help with giving tankier meatshields some extra hits to stall. Overall, a great Metal Cyclone killer and a somewhat useful debuffer.
*[[Agent Staal (Uber Rare Cat)|Edgemaster Staal]]: Can Slow every enemy on the stage with near-perfect uptime, and has both Z-Kill and Critical abilities. With a few Cat Combos or minimal support, he's basically a free win.
*[[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]]: If one is lucky enough to have her, she can make this stage almost trivial with her Critical Hit and Zombie Killer abilities. Just be sure to protect her blindspot with debuffers like Puppetmaster & Charlie and Ectoweight Cat.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: With only Metal and Zombie enemies in this stage, they can apply constant knockback and help you gain ground.

